---js
{
  layout: "layouts/base.njk",
  pagination: { data: "nhtsa.models", size: 1, alias: "hub", addAllPagesToCollections: true },
  permalink: (data) => data.hub.url,
  eleventyComputed: {
    title: (data) => `${data.hub.name} problems by year: complaints and recalls ${data.hub.range}`,
    description: (data) => {
      const h = data.hub, w = h.rankable[0], b = h.rankable.at(-1);
      return `${h.name} owner complaints and recalls for every model year ${h.range}, from NHTSA data. Most complaints: ${w.year} (${w.s.total.toLocaleString("en-US")}). Fewest: ${b.year} (${b.s.total.toLocaleString("en-US")}).`;
    },
    faqs: (data) => {
      const h = data.hub, w = h.rankable[0], b = h.rankable.at(-1), fmt = (n) => n.toLocaleString("en-US");
      const byRecalls = [...h.years].sort((x, y) => y.s.recalls.length - x.s.recalls.length)[0];
      return [
        { q: `Which ${h.name} model year has the most owner complaints?`, a: `${w.year}, with ${fmt(w.s.total)} complaints in NHTSA's data (owners name ${w.s.named[0]?.label.toLowerCase()} most often). That is a raw count among model years ${h.range}. It is not adjusted for sales or age, and it is not a reliability or safety ranking.` },
        { q: `Which ${h.name} year has the fewest complaints?`, a: `${b.year}, with ${fmt(b.s.total)} complaints among model years ${h.range} that are not flagged as API gaps. Fewer complaints is not a reliability or safety ranking.` },
        { q: `Which ${h.name} years should I avoid?`, a: `This site does not publish an avoid list. NHTSA does not rate reliability, and complaint counts are not adjusted for how many cars were sold or how old they are. What the data does show: the raw complaint count is highest for ${w.year} (${fmt(w.s.total)}) and lowest for ${b.year} (${fmt(b.s.total)}), and ${byRecalls.year} has the most recall campaigns (${byRecalls.s.recalls.length}). The table above lists every year. For a specific car, check its VIN at nhtsa.gov/recalls and have it inspected.` },
        (() => {
          const tally = new Map();
          for (const y of h.years) for (const c of (y.s.named || [])) tally.set(c.label, (tally.get(c.label) || 0) + c.count);
          const top = [...tally.entries()].sort((x, y) => y[1] - x[1]).slice(0, 3);
          return top.length ? { q: `What are the most common problems with the ${h.name}?`, a: `Across model years ${h.range}, owners most often name ${top.map(([l, n]) => `${l.toLowerCase()} (${fmt(n)})`).join(", ")} in NHTSA complaints. A complaint can name more than one component, so counts overlap, and they are unverified owner allegations rather than confirmed defects. The table above shows each year's most-named component.` } : null;
        })(),
        { q: `Which ${h.name} year has the most recalls?`, a: `${byRecalls.year}, with ${byRecalls.s.recalls.length} recall campaigns in NHTSA's recall database. A campaign may cover only some vehicles of that model year. Check a VIN at nhtsa.gov/recalls.` },
      ].filter(Boolean);
    },
    crumbs: (data) => [{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: data.hub.make, url: `/${data.hub.makeSlug}/` }, { name: data.hub.model }],
  },
}
---
{%- set w = hub.rankable[0] -%}{%- set b = hub.rankable | last -%}
<p class="kicker"><a href="/{{ hub.makeSlug }}/">{{ hub.make }}</a></p>
<h1>{{ hub.name }} problems by model year</h1>
<p class="last-checked">NHTSA data checked {{ hub.checked | prettyDate }}</p>
<section class="quick" aria-labelledby="sum">
<h2 id="sum">Summary</h2>
<p>Across model years {{ hub.range }}, NHTSA's public databases list {{ hub.totalComplaints | n }} owner complaints and {{ hub.totalRecalls }} distinct recall campaigns for the {{ hub.name }}.</p>
<p>The year with the most complaints is <strong>{{ w.year }}</strong> ({{ w.s.total | n }}; owners name {{ w.s.named[0].label | lower }} most). The year with the fewest is <strong>{{ b.year }}</strong> ({{ b.s.total | n }}). The median year has {{ hub.medianComplaints | n }}.</p>
<p>These are raw counts. They are not a reliability or safety ranking, they are not adjusted for how many of each year were sold, and older years have had longer to collect complaints.</p>
</section>

<h2 id="years">Every model year</h2>
<div class="tablewrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Model year</th><th class="num">Complaints</th><th class="num">Recalls</th><th class="num">Crash</th><th class="num">Fire</th><th>Most-named component</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for y in hub.years %}<tr{% if y.suspectGap %} class="flag"{% endif %}><td>{% if y.featured %}<a href="/{{ hub.makeSlug }}/{{ hub.modelSlug }}/{{ y.year }}/">{{ y.year }}</a>{% else %}{{ y.year }}{% endif %}{% if y.noRecords %} — no NHTSA records (likely not sold as this model year){% elif y.suspectGap %} — NHTSA's API count looks incomplete{% endif %}</td><td class="num">{{ y.s.total | n }}</td><td class="num">{{ y.s.recalls.length }}</td><td class="num">{{ y.s.crash | n }}</td><td class="num">{{ y.s.fire | n }}</td><td>{{ y.s.named[0].label if y.s.named.length else "—" }}{% if y.s.named.length %} <span class="muted">({{ y.s.named[0].share }}%)</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
<p class="muted">Linked years have a full page with every component and recall. Other years get pages over time; the counts above are already live.{% if hub.years | selectattr("suspectGap") | length %} Highlighted rows look like gaps in what NHTSA's API returns for that year, not a quiet year; they are left out of the complaint-count order.{% endif %}</p>
{% if hub.topics.length %}
<h2 id="components">Component pages</h2>
<ul class="cards">
{% for t in hub.topics %}<li><a href="{{ t.url }}"><strong>{{ t.label }}</strong><span>{{ t.complaintNaming | n }} complaints name this group · {{ t.recalls.length }} matching recall campaigns</span></a></li>{% endfor %}
</ul>
<p class="muted">A component page follows one NHTSA group across model years. Complaint counts and recall campaigns stay separate, and neither is a reliability ranking.</p>
{% endif %}

{% include "partials/faq.njk" %}

<section class="sources" aria-labelledby="src">
<h2 id="src">Sources</h2>
<p>Each count comes from NHTSA's Complaints API (complaintsByVehicle) and Recalls API (recallsByVehicle) for make {{ hub.years[0].rec.nhtsa_make }}, model {{ hub.years[0].rec.nhtsa_model }}, one request per model year, for example <a href="{{ w.rec.complaints_source_url }}" rel="nofollow noopener">{{ w.rec.complaints_source_url }}</a>. Checked {{ hub.checked }}. See <a href="/about/">method</a>.</p>
</section>
